00:00:05.749 --> 00:00:07.430 align:start position:0%
eu fisheries ministers hope to reach a  political agreement on quotas for  catches of certain fish species in the  baltic sea for next year when they meet  in luxembourg on october 17.  the european commission is proposing  maximum quantities for specific kinds of  fish including herring cod salmon and  spratt taking into account the latest  scientific advice and reports by key  fisheries and maritime organizations  in the case of cod quotas are  established in line with a specific  long-term plan to ensure that stocks in  the baltic sea are not depleted  the plan includes limits for the number  of days at sea authorized for this kind  of fishing  the catch limits data is supposed to be  made available to fishermen in the  baltic by the 1st of january next year  the ministers will also hold an exchange  of views on the annual consultations  between the eu and norway on the  management of shared fish stocks such as  those in the north sea and skagerek  size of annual catch quantities on seven  species including cod haddock herring  whiting and shrimp are jointly agreed  between the two at the moment  the ministers will also hold an exchange  of views ahead of the annual meeting of  the international commission for the  conservation of atlantic tunas which  will take place from the 18th to the  25th of november in south africa  the organization's work has an impact on  the management of among other species  bluefin tuna in the atlantic and the  mediterranean and this has important  implications for the fishing industry in  the eu and the preservation of stocks
 

